       id="plugins" title="Extending the engine">

    <section-starting-page>
        <title>Extending the engine</title>
        <description>
            A <code>WeaverPlugin</code> adds behaviour to the weaver itself: new places an
            injection may name, new kinds of injection, metadata on every class it stamps. It is
            neither the Maven plugin nor the IDE plugin. It compiles against
            <code>aether-weaver-api</code> and names no engine type.
        </description>

        <spotlight>
            <a href="what-a-plugin-can-do.topic" type="idea"
               summary="What the six registrations accept, and why only a weaver your own program builds ever loads one">What a plugin can do</a>
            <a href="write-a-plugin.topic" type="creative"
               summary="One class, one identity, one contribute call. The smallest plugin the engine will accept">Write a plugin</a>
        </spotlight>

        <primary>
            <title>Loading a plugin, and what it contributes</title>
            <a href="plugin-lifecycle.topic" type="mixed"
               summary="The four gates a candidate passes before it contributes, and the events it hears afterwards">The plugin lifecycle</a>
